{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Living the Dream"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Did It!"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le16ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Causative Get and Have"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use a causative verb when we want to talk about something that someone else did for us. It means that the subject caused the action to happen, but didn't do it themselves. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the causative verbs <span class=\"strong\">get/have </span> when you want to make it clear that the subject paid, asked, or persuaded the other person to do something. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes, you use <span class=\"italic\">get </span> when you want to convey the feeling that you need to convince someone to do something. <span class=\"italic\">Have </span> is a little more neutral."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My last supervisor got her editors to be extremely precise."}, {"type": "example", "content": "My colleague had the two of us take a seminar in time management"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'll only get you to answer two more questions. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think I got you to answer everything. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Get\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" [get + person + to + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got her to work</span>  late on Tuesday.<br> Did the boss <span class=\\\"strong\\\">get you to work </span> on Saturday?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to convince to do something or to trick someone into doing something.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"[get + object + past participle]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">got my jacket cleaned</span> before the meeting. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more informal way of saying that someone else did something for you (it focuses on object not the subject)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"[have + object + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Dr. Smith <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had his nurse take</span>  the patient's temperature.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to give someone the responsibility to do something.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" [have + person + verb]\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had the hairdresser style</span> my hair for me. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to give someone the responsibility to do something on your behalf\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">what-clauses </span> are used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasise what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">what-clauses</span>  which are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is </span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span> ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I now need <span class=\"strong\">is</span>  a new car.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">A new car is <span class=\"strong\">what I </span> now need.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>,  <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">loathe</span>, <span class=\"strong\"> love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, <span class=\"strong\">want</span>.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "What-clauses are also often used with <span class=\"strong\">does</span> /<span class=\"strong\">do</span> /<span class=\"strong\">did </span> <span class=\"strong\">and </span> when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> the manager <span class=\"strong\">did </span> first <span class=\"strong\">was </span> interview all the salespeople </span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What we do here is often very stressful."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What I want is a job that is tailored to my competencies and which includes writing and editing. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "What I think is my greatest strength is my writing skills. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "imminent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "happening very soon"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The website says the launch of several new books is imminent. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you negotiate a salary."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attention to detail"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "noticing small, specific things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have strong attention to detail when it comes to my writing."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "thrive"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do well"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thrived under quick deadlines and multiple projects. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le16ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "launch"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to start up"}, {"type": "part_speech", 